  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABKCh-CQ",
      "title": "ops: keep genesis files as opaque JSON",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 1384,
      "body": "Stacked on #1382 (needs its monorepo bump for `op-core/genesis`).\n\nThe registry no longer uses op-geth's genesis types: it keeps genesis files as opaque JSON, validates them with op-core, and writes op-deployer's genesis as is. Decoding through `core.Genesis` keeps only the fields the linked geth knows, and upstream go-ethereum's chain config has no OP fields (`optimism`, `regolithTime`…`jovianTime`, `bedrockBlock`), so on upstream geth these would be dropped silently from every genesis the registry publishes.\n\n- `ReadGenesis`/`WriteGenesis` (used by `sync_staging`) keep the genesis JSON byte for byte. `TestGenesisRoundTrip` round-trips every file under `superchain/extra/genesis` and checks the bytes are unchanged; some files are pretty-printed, so a decode and re-encode would not keep them.\n- `ValidateGenesisIntegrity` builds an `op-core/params.ChainConfig` from the chain's TOML and compares `op-core/genesis.ToBlock().Hash()` instead of hand-building an op-geth config. Every chain `check_genesis_integrity` checks still matches its hash. op-core rejects `stateHash`, which only the legacy-migrated chains the check already skips use.\n- `create_config` writes `op-deployer inspect genesis` output compacted, which keeps its key order (go-ethereum's `core.Genesis` order). This drops `opaqueToGenesis` and its losslessness check. Unlike before, an old op-deployer's `terminalTotalDifficultyPassed` is kept and op-geth's `\"slotNumber\":null` is no longer added.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T14:05:04Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 236,
      "deletions": 196
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABKChpQA",
      "title": "ops: bump monorepo to develop and switch to op-service/log",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 1382,
      "body": "Bumps `ops` to monorepo develop at ethereum-optimism/optimism@fbfb3587c9 (ethereum-optimism/optimism#23527) and op-geth to `v1.101702.4-rc.1`, the version that commit pins.\n\n- ethereum-optimism/optimism#23527 moved op-fetcher's library: the `fetch/script` types are now in `op-fetcher/chaininfo` (`ChainConfig` → `Config`, `CreateChainConfig(out)` → `out.Config()`), with the same JSON shape. op-fetcher now reads chain info with `eth_call`s instead of a forge script. A full `codegen` run against public L1 RPCs gives the same output on this branch as on `main`.\n- `fetch.NewFetcher` now takes `op-service/log`'s `Logger`, so `ops` logs through `op-service/log` instead of `go-ethereum/log`.\n- The `validation` requirement in `ops/go.mod` moves up to the version the monorepo requires. `ops/go.work` still resolves it to the local module.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T14:04:41Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-23T09:32:05Z",
      "additions": 104,
      "deletions": 141
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABKCh7yA",
      "title": "ops: read superchain.toml from disk for the standard state",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 1383,
      "body": "`ops` took the standard op-deployer state's SuperchainConfig address from op-geth's `superchain` package, which embeds a copy of this registry's own configs. It now reads `superchain/configs/{mainnet,sepolia}/superchain.toml` from the repo. To find it, the state mergers, `OpDeployer` and the staging report now take the repo root.\n\nThis uses the registry's current data instead of a stale copy. The pinned op-geth embeds a snapshot of this repo from June. A change to a network's `superchain_config_addr` used to take effect only after a new op-geth snapshot and an op-geth bump. Now it applies in the same PR, and a network that isn't in the snapshot works too. Today the values are the same for both networks, and `TestMergeState`'s golden output covers sepolia.\n\nThis was the only op-geth-only package `ops` imported.\n\nConflicts with #1382 in the `deployer_test.go` imports only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T14:05:01Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-23T12:15:45Z",
      "additions": 57,
      "deletions": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABKCcMng",
      "title": "Add kona-client v1.8.1-rc.1 and v1.8.1 prestates",
      "author": "pauldowman",
      "number": 1381,
      "body": "Adds the reproducible `cannon64-kona` and `cannon64-kona-interop` prestates for kona-client v1.8.1-rc.1 and v1.8.1, the v1.8 backport release for the eMudhra CA distrust (ethereum-optimism/optimism#23566, ethereum-optimism/optimism#23567) and the go1.26.10 toolchain bump (ethereum-optimism/optimism#23546).\n\n- Both tags point at the same commit (`739d6110ca`), so the two versions carry the same hashes. They were built with `just reproducible-kona-prestate` at that commit.\n- The hashes are identical to v1.8.0, because the backport only changes the images' trust store and toolchain, not the kona-client program.\n- Both hashes are published in the prestate bucket.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T13:58:25Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-22T14:32:06Z",
